---
scope: "Making the Intelligence Console the ENTRY POINT to a harnessed Intelligence. When no instance is CONNECTED — which means REACHABLE (`channel/alive`) *and* HARNESSED (`self/daemons[intelligence_launcher]`), because a bare `claude` with the channel MCP publishes a perfect heartbeat and still cannot self-compact — the context pane swaps its frozen gauge for a Launch affordance; pressing it publishes an `_app/intelligence/open` intent that the EXISTING `app_launcher` daemon turns into a TERMINAL running the launcher harness (a human terminal must exist, because the launcher is a transparent PTY proxy and the human answers Claude Code's startup dialogs). Covers the two-signal presence model and its four states, the swap mechanism, the launch intent + its control-is-a-peer dedupe, the terminal spawn, the cold-start-with-bootstrap rule, the launch cwd, the singleton's flip from supersede to yield-if-held, the `degraded` third verdict value with its triggers, hysteresis and rendering, and the two-tier acceptance bar."
audience: "The builder wiring the launch affordance + the app_launcher terminal target; the composeux-architect, who has now closed the last of this spec's decision points (there are ZERO open); anyone who later asks why the console spawns a Terminal instead of a headless child, or why a fresh heartbeat is not enough to call an Intelligence connected."
boundary: "IN: the TWO-SIGNAL presence model + its staleness and unknown rules ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE]); the `degraded` THIRD verdict value — its two triggers, its hysteresis, its rendering on the header + the gauge card, and its own slice ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE], [DD-ICL-DEGRADED], [CXC-ICL-SLICES] slice 5); the four states + the swap mechanism ([CXC-ICL-VISIBILITY], [CXC-ICL-PANE-SWAP], [CXC-ICL-PANEL]); the `_app/intelligence/open` intent + payload + the harness-keyed peer guard ([CXC-ICL-INTENT], [CXC-ICL-PEER-GUARD]); the spawn-once dedupe reusing `spawned_windows` ([CXC-ICL-SPAWN-ONCE]); the singleton re-ratification and the retirement of the CLI entry point ([CXC-ICL-SINGLETON-YIELD], [CXC-ICL-CLI-UNSUPPORTED]); the terminal spawn, the launch cwd, the cold-start-with-bootstrap rule, the one entry script ([CXC-ICL-TERMINAL], [CXC-ICL-CWD], [CXC-ICL-COLD], [CXC-ICL-ENTRY]); the error/boundary matrix and the acceptance bar. OUT: the `/compact` actuation relay itself ([CXC-IC-LIFECYCLE] — consumed, never changed); the launcher's PTY proxy internals and its harness monitor ([CXC-IC-MONITOR]); `daemon_watch`'s own probe logic (consumed, never changed); the headless multi-intelligence fleet spawner ([CXC-IH-HOST], whose `interactive` mode explicitly defers to the launcher — see [CXC-ICL-SCOPE-BOUNDARY]); the fleet roster UI ([CXC-IH-CONSOLE]); the Launch Bar's `_app/harness/open` FOCUS tile ([CXC-LB-ROSTER] tile 2 — untouched, and distinct: see [DD-ICL-INTENT-KEY]); RESUMING a specific prior session ([CXC-ICL-COLD]); the terminal widget that may one day host the PTY in-console ([SPEC:CXC-TERM] — cross-referenced, not specified here)."
not-this: "Not a new spawner — `intelligence/tools/app_launcher.py` gains ONE table row, a payload argument, and a launch handle ([CXC-ICL-TERMINAL], [CXC-ICL-SPAWN-ONCE]); no second launch daemon is created ([DD-LB-LAUNCH-MECHANISM] holds). Not a new liveness namespace or a new harness prober — BOTH signals exist and are already on the bus (`channel/alive` via `channel_bridge`, `self/daemons` via `daemon_watch`); the console READS them and mints nothing ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE]). Not a ONE-signal presence model — a fresh heartbeat proves REACHABLE, never HARNESSED, and a design that conflates them hides the button in exactly the case it was built for. Not a new dedupe mechanism — `spawned_windows` already implements spawn-once and is already the shared seam ([CXC-ICL-SPAWN-ONCE]). Not a `launching` pane state — the anti-double-spawn guarantee lives in the daemon, where it also covers the bus path ([DD-ICL-NO-LAUNCHING-STATE]). Not an auto-answered startup dialog — keystroke injection into Claude Code's TUI dialogs was tried, collided with the human, and hung ([CXC-ICL-CONSTRAINT-PTY]); it stays out of scope forever. Not an engine addition — the pane swap uses `ordered_stack`'s existing `visibility_namespace` ([SPEC:CXC-ORDER])."
depends-on: [34-composeux-intelligence-console.lts, 41-intelligence-host-spawner.lts, 48-compose-launch-bar.lts]
