**Version**: 0.6
**Created**: 2026-08-10
**Updated**: 2026-08-11 (v0.6) — [CXC-ICL-COLD] amended to follow the terminal widget's FIRST LIVE SPAWN, with the node's RULE unchanged and only its delivery mechanism replaced: the bootstrap now rides the child's POSITIONAL PROMPT ARGUMENT and `BOOTSTRAP_DELAY` / the settle timer / the whole startup-injection path are DELETED ([CXC-TERM-BOOTSTRAP-ARGV], [CXC-TERM-BOOTSTRAP-SETTLE-RETIRED]); manifest resolution becomes a CHAIN — `META_MANIFEST` then `<id>.meta.json` then `<role>.meta.json` then a LOUD refusal ([CXC-TERM-MANIFEST-CHAIN]) — because a hosted child now carries an id distinct from its host's ([CXC-TERM-CHILD-ID]). The scenario that read "the launcher types the re-register bootstrap after `BOOTSTRAP_DELAY`" is corrected, and the now-inverted `BOOTSTRAP_DELAY` verify is named as a known-gap rather than quietly re-scoped.
**Updated**: 2026-08-10 (v0.2) — folded in David's three corrections: the re-register bootstrap is DEFAULT (cold start is the settled choice, [CXC-ICL-COLD], [DD-ICL-COLD-VS-RESUME]); the terminal-spawn reuse is ratified ([CXC-ICL-TERMINAL]); the LAUNCHING pane state is REMOVED and spawn-once moved into the daemon via `spawned_windows` ([CXC-ICL-VISIBILITY], [CXC-ICL-SPAWN-ONCE], [DD-ICL-NO-LAUNCHING-STATE]).
**Updated**: 2026-08-10 (v0.3) — TWO-SIGNAL presence, verified live: `channel/alive` proves REACHABLE, `self/daemons[intelligence_launcher]` proves HARNESSED, and only both mean CONNECTED ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE]); four named states with `unharnessed` as the case the feature exists for ([CXC-ICL-VISIBILITY]); the peer guard re-keyed onto HARNESSED, not reachable ([CXC-ICL-PEER-GUARD]); the launcher singleton re-ratified from SUPERSEDE to YIELD-IF-HELD + LOUD ([CXC-ICL-SINGLETON-YIELD]) and CLI `transport.sh` retired as a supported entry point ([CXC-ICL-CLI-UNSUPPORTED]), cross-referenced to [CXC-TERM-SINGLETON] in [SPEC:CXC-TERM] so the resolution is recorded once.
**Updated**: 2026-08-10 (v0.4) — FOUR decision points CLOSED against David's Decision-Support-Doc (`docs/intelligence-console/DECISIONS-ic-launch-and-conops.md`, recorded on every closed node as `dsd-source`): [DD-ICL-UNHARNESSED-ACTION] RESOLVED as alternative (c) — a state-2 launch goes out under the DISTINCT id `recovery-architect-2` and the state is reframed as a RECOVERY/fallback mode, which dissolves (c)'s identity-fragmentation cost and closes the shared-id clobber BY CONSTRUCTION ([CXC-ICL-VISIBILITY] state 2, [CXC-ICL-PANEL] body, [CXC-ICL-BOUNDARIES] row 15, plus a recorded-not-taken `channel_bridge` prevention note); [DD-ICL-DEGRADED] REVERSED from DEFERRED to RESOLVED alternative (a) — `degraded` becomes a THIRD value of `link_health`'s single verdict, read by BOTH the header dot and the pane, never derived twice ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE]); [DD-ICL-LAUNCH-HINT] RESOLVED as the recommended YES — the 90 s `LAUNCH_HINT_S` sub-line ships, behaviour-free by construction ([CXC-ICL-PANEL]); and [DD-ICL-PANE-OWNER] RESOLVED as PROPOSED, ratified by the ARCHITECT rather than David because both alternatives were already self-rejected in its own text.
**Updated**: 2026-08-10 (v0.5) — the LAST decision point closed, and the `degraded` residual retired: [DD-ICL-INTENT-KEY] RESOLVED as the PROPOSED form — a NEW target key `intelligence`, ratified by the composeux-ARCHITECT and not by David (he settled four other calls here via his DSD; this one is the architect's, and the provenance is recorded so it cannot be misread), leaving `_app/harness/open`'s FOCUS/HOST semantics untouched; and `degraded` — which David promoted from DEFERRED to shipping in DSD D2 ([DD-ICL-DEGRADED]) but which no slice and no acceptance criterion carried — now has its OWN slice 5 ([CXC-ICL-SLICES], split on the one-pass test, not on caution), a ratified rendering that resolves as `reachable = yes` and therefore never withholds the gauge and never reveals the launch button ([CXC-ICL-PRESENCE], [CXC-ICL-VISIBILITY] — no fifth row), concrete PROVISIONAL triggers with hysteresis (`DEGRADED_CLIMB_N` 3 / `DEGRADED_RECOVER_N` 1) and the offline-beats-degraded precedence cascade, the newly-named `map:`-fallback hazard on `console/link/state`'s other bound consumers, and acceptance criteria ICL-C17..C20 plus [CXC-ICL-BOUNDARIES] rows 16-17.
**Status**: Draft — ZERO open decision points: every `DD-ICL-` decision node in section 9 carries `status: resolved`, and `degraded` now carries both a slice and acceptance criteria. Ready for dispatch.
